# Append-only event ledgers (NDJSON) — every branch appends distinct lines, so a
# default merge treats them as conflicting edits to the same region. `merge=union`
# keeps BOTH sides' lines (no conflict markers) — correct for append-only logs.
# Codified 2026-05-30 after a lingering vector-costs.ndjson merge conflict blocked
# the Phase 3 integration (learn-from-gating: a recurring gate is a fix, not a chore).
project-history/vector-costs.ndjson      merge=union
project-history/auto-improvement.ndjson  merge=union
project-history/*.ndjson                 merge=union

# Docs carrying auto-generated `<!-- kb-counts:start:X -->…:end:X -->` inventory
# blocks. The counts are DETERMINISTICALLY regenerated from the tree by the
# pre-commit hook + auto-staged into every commit, so two parallel branches that
# each add files to the SAME product both bump the same inventory row/grand-total
# → a default 3-way merge reports a conflict on pure machine churn (observed
# 2026-06-05 integrating two file-disjoint social-wiring branches). `union` is
# WRONG here (it duplicates table rows); instead the `kb-counts` driver
# re-derives the block from the merged tree (correct) and still surfaces any
# genuine PROSE conflict outside the blocks. Driver = scripts/hooks/merge-kb-counts.sh,
# registered (local git config) by scripts/hooks/install-hooks.sh.
# KB § PATTERNS/common/auto-generated-merge-drivers.md
KNOWLEDGE-BASE/CONTEXT/02-LANDSCAPE.md   merge=kb-counts
KNOWLEDGE-BASE/CONTEXT/06-AGENTS.md      merge=kb-counts
KNOWLEDGE-BASE/AGENT-CONTEXT.md          merge=kb-counts
